=== Test 24: Correlated scalar subquery — less than ===
o_total < (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
SUM per orderkey: (1,300),(2,200),(3,550),(4,200),(5,750)
Only order 5 qualifies (400 < 750)
== Query ==
SELECT o_id, SUM(o_total)
FROM orders
WHERE o_total < (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
GROUP BY o_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 2

== Diff ==
==========




=== Test 25: Correlated scalar subquery — equality ===
o_total = (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
Only order 4 qualifies (200 = 200)
== Query ==
SELECT o_id, SUM(o_total)
FROM orders
WHERE o_total = (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
GROUP BY o_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 2

== Diff ==
==========




=== Test 26: Correlated scalar subquery — greater than ===
o_total > (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
Orders 1,2,3 qualify: (500>300, 300>200, 700>550)
== Query ==
SELECT o_id, SUM(o_total)
FROM orders
WHERE o_total > (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
GROUP BY o_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 4

== Diff ==
==========




=== Test 27: Correlated scalar subquery with outer filter ===
o_custkey = 200 AND o_total > SUM(l_price): only order 3 (700>550)
== Query ==
SELECT o_id, SUM(o_total)
FROM orders
WHERE o_custkey = 200
AND o_total > (SELECT SUM(l_price) FROM lineitem WHERE l_orderkey = o_id)
GROUP BY o_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 2

